1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,297
In eighth grade, I walked a long way to
school.

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,625
Our road crossed a wide field.

3
00:00:08,625 --> 00:00:11,444
One day, walking home with my friends…

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:16,315
we found a hobbled horse in the field.

5
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:21,099
“Let's ride it!” we said.

6
00:00:21,099 --> 00:00:23,409
My friends held my satchel for me.

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:27,091
We surrounded it and caught it.

8
00:00:27,091 --> 00:00:29,982
I tied its mouth with the hobble rope
and climbed on.

9
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,960
When I said “Go!”, it ran like the wind.

10
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:40,828
I tried to stop it; it refused.

11
00:00:40,828 --> 00:00:42,629
The rope was no bridle.

12
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:46,665
It carried me into someone's teff.

13
00:00:46,665 --> 00:00:49,263
My friends panicked, shouting “Let go!”

14
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:54,228
Then I saw the owner coming from far
away.

15
00:00:56,400 --> 00:01:01,035
As it raced on, I jumped off and landed
in the mud on purpose.

16
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:06,553
It was tsedey, the ground was soft, and
I wasn't hurt.

17
00:01:06,553 --> 00:01:08,188
My friends were so relieved.

18
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,496
We ran off together, and the owner never
got to beat us.

19
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:20,439
Even today, when we meet, we remember
that horse and laugh.
